<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Sign in with Apple. Wired via CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS in ios/project.yml. It sits HERE rather than in App/ for the
  same reason Biyaherong.storekit does: everything under App/ is swept into the target by the
  `- path: App` source entry, and an entitlements plist copied into the app bundle as a resource
  is not what anybody wants. Out here it needs an explicit entry with `buildPhase: none`.

  Committed rather than generated from XcodeGen's `entitlements:` block, for the same reason the
  app icon catalog is committed (see the comment beside ASSETCATALOG_COMPILER_APPICON_NAME): a
  build whose entitlement file is missing still succeeds, and the failure only shows up at runtime
  as a sheet that never appears.

  This file alone is not enough. The capability must ALSO be enabled for the App ID
  (com.prince24pogi.biyaherongchessapp) in the Apple Developer portal, or signing fails outright.
  And note the free CI path — codemagic.yaml's `ios-free-unsigned` — archives with
  CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO, so entitlements are never applied there: that .ipa compiles but cannot
  sign in. Use `ios-testflight` to test the login. See ios/BUILD-iOS.md.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
